<title>NEW ZEALAND: Record volume traded on NZFOE.</title>
<headline>Record volume traded on NZFOE.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>A record total of 12,451 bill futures contracts traded on the New Zealand Futures and Options Exchanges on Thursday, the exchange said.</p>
<p>It beat the previous total of 10,843 traded on June 11, 1997, a closeout day.</p>
<p>Trading was boosted today by a comment from Reserve Bank Governor Don Brash that monetary conditions were too easy.</p>
<p>The September contract fell 18 points to 92.85 on volume of 10,611.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
